#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186324594 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c30217a-484c-5c31-a2bf-413f04e0edea" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Triangle Given Its Vertices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "204ec977-b1ba-5c6f-9231-575c58f156dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324596} {:answer/id #uuid "756736f5-f53e-5f2e-845c-b194756d5650" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324597} {:answer/id #uuid "2f78357d-0ab4-5517-ad10-1ff518f19027" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324598} {:answer/id #uuid "3ba431f3-3db3-5f36-905b-50991616823b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324599} {:answer/id #uuid "0b628283-4da3-5123-b0f0-2a6ba0715389" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324600}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "204ec977-b1ba-5c6f-9231-575c58f156dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324596} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb2eddcf-f48f-5705-a434-dcc471f726e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324595}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "588b7ac8-1d13-58bf-8be3-40e1395c4ae0" :question/math-academy-id "q-127915" :question/problem "Calculate the area of the $△\\,WXY,$ if $W(3,9,4),$ $X(1,7,3),$ $Y(6,12,8).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{WX}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{WY}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{WX} & =x-w \\\\  & =(i+7j+3k)-(3i+9j+4k) \\\\  & =-2i-2j-k \\\\  & =⟨-2,-2,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{WY} & =y-w \\\\  & =(6i+12j+8k)-(3i+9j+4k) \\\\  & =3i+3j+4k \\\\  & =⟨3,3,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{WX}\\times \\overset{\\to }{WY} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-2)\\cdot 4-3\\cdot (-1))i-((-2)\\cdot 4-3\\cdot (-1))j+((-2)\\cdot 3-3\\cdot (-2))k \\\\  & =-5i+5j \\\\  & =⟨-5,5,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{WX}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{WY}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{WX}\\times \\overset{\\to }{WY}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-5)^{2}+{5}^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,WXY$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{5\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186350575 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9331987e-8676-5bdb-b4ce-2129b1b09a8c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Altitude of a Triangle Given Its Vertices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f99fa164-3ecd-58bc-bb9b-7d8bd15a74d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6\\sqrt{38}}{19}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350577} {:answer/id #uuid "c68f18a2-3893-5427-b42d-b8f9d6de0c84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{38}}{19}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350578} {:answer/id #uuid "e4117b44-4102-5187-bcac-f2523568816b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350579} {:answer/id #uuid "97251a72-fab3-5254-9542-9838d7075a30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350580} {:answer/id #uuid "7418b660-2b11-5e72-a772-fe83e24dbce2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{38}}{38}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350581}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f99fa164-3ecd-58bc-bb9b-7d8bd15a74d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6\\sqrt{38}}{19}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350577} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d873505-a18c-5dbd-b872-957b944e5ae6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350576}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0a2fce35-3849-53f0-9cee-8dbfca3f9123" :question/math-academy-id "q-128008" :question/problem "Calculate the length of the altitude $RH$ of the $△\\,PRQ,$ if $P(3,0,4),$ $Q(2,3,1),$ $R(0,3,1).$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the length of the altitude $RH$ can be related to the area of $△\\,PQR$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}RH\\cdot PQ\n$$\n\nSo, to find $RH,$ we first find ${A}_{△}.$ To start, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =q-p \\\\  & =(2i+3j+k)-(3i+4k) \\\\  & =-i+3j-3j \\\\  & =⟨-1,3,-3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{PR} & =r-p \\\\  & =(3j+k)-(3i+4k) \\\\  & =-3i+3j-3k \\\\  & =⟨-3,3,-3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\times \\overset{\\to }{PR} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & 3 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 3 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ -3 & -3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 3\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(3\\cdot (-3)-3\\cdot (-3))i-((-1)\\cdot (-3)-(-3)\\cdot (-3))j+((-1)\\cdot 3-(-3)\\cdot 3)k \\\\  & =6j+6k \\\\  & =⟨0,6,6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\times \\overset{\\to }{PR}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{6}^{2}+{6}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{72} \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,PQR$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{6\\sqrt{2}}{2}=3\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's also compute $PQ$ since it appears in the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}PQ & =|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{3}^{2}+(-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{19}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, using the formula ${A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}RH\\cdot PQ,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△} & =\\frac{1}{2}RH\\cdot PQ \\\\ 3\\sqrt{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}RH\\cdot \\sqrt{19} \\\\ 6\\sqrt{2} & =RH\\cdot \\sqrt{19} \\\\ RH & =\\frac{6\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{19}} \\\\ RH & =\\frac{6\\sqrt{38}}{19}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186350582 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c30217a-484c-5c31-a2bf-413f04e0edea" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Triangle Given Its Vertices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18bd6986-6612-50cc-9393-633e1ad7b0af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{34}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350584}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "18bd6986-6612-50cc-9393-633e1ad7b0af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{34}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350584} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e19f751-c1b4-57d2-bbd0-dfd1ae8c4f82" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350583}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cdc31bfd-d117-59f8-a541-105b7e8c3a1d" :question/math-academy-id "q-275224" :question/problem "Calculate the area ${A}_{△}$ of the $△\\,ABC$, if $A(-2,0,-1)$, $B(-3,3,-4)$, $C(0,-2,2).$\n\n${A}_{△}=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(-3i+3j-4k)-(-2i-k) \\\\  & =-i+3j-3k \\\\  & =⟨-1,3,-3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(-2j+2k)-(-2i-k) \\\\  & =2i-2j+3k \\\\  & =⟨2,-2,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(3\\cdot 3-(-2)\\cdot (-3))i-((-1)\\cdot 3-2\\cdot (-3))j+((-1)\\cdot (-2)-2\\cdot 3)k \\\\  & =3i-3j-4k \\\\  & =⟨3,-3,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{34}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,ABC$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{\\sqrt{34}}{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186350585 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c30217a-484c-5c31-a2bf-413f04e0edea" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Triangle Given Its Vertices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6f48f53a-d894-5bbd-9f36-536d63f2f504" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350587} {:answer/id #uuid "598e7301-6927-57fb-bc92-0a4083fcf305" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350588} {:answer/id #uuid "d9b54c36-462c-5b60-a404-ba5758ad9cdc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350589} {:answer/id #uuid "70d8df7e-12a5-5b86-a882-82e39b214fb9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350590} {:answer/id #uuid "a243e64e-7333-5802-a918-eda68b1776c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350591}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70d8df7e-12a5-5b86-a882-82e39b214fb9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350590} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6e5aac2-ca9b-54d9-ad9e-5218bc54c3e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350586}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6d2a2f20-248d-5b98-87d8-9cde9ba325b0" :question/math-academy-id "q-71107" :question/problem "Calculate the area of the $△\\,NPQ$, if $N(1,0,1)$, $P(2,2,3)$, $Q(2,1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{NP}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{NQ}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{NP} & =p-n \\\\  & =(2i+2j+3k)-(i+k) \\\\  & =i+2j+2k \\\\  & =⟨1,2,2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{NQ} & =q-n \\\\  & =(2i+j+k)-(i+k) \\\\  & =i+j \\\\  & =⟨1,1,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{NP}\\times \\overset{\\to }{NQ} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(2\\cdot 0-1\\cdot 2)i-(1\\cdot 0-1\\cdot 2)j+(1\\cdot 1-1\\cdot 2)k \\\\  & =-2i+2j-k \\\\  & =⟨-2,2,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{NP}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{NQ}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{NP}\\times \\overset{\\to }{NQ}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,NPQ$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{3}{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186350592 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9331987e-8676-5bdb-b4ce-2129b1b09a8c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Altitude of a Triangle Given Its Vertices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b256a0a-54e3-5d07-80c5-191df4988e7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350594} {:answer/id #uuid "4eb47461-13a6-5780-a4bd-29971a889db0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350595} {:answer/id #uuid "265b81e4-19d2-5a40-8a13-9c354b376b25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350596} {:answer/id #uuid "aaaaa3dc-5197-585c-b6e8-ca4fc16a55f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{6}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350597} {:answer/id #uuid "9252b8ff-c040-5ba0-a4c0-5954d9283633" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350598}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "265b81e4-19d2-5a40-8a13-9c354b376b25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350596} :answer-field/id #uuid "50b84d81-dbab-5875-acb8-1712fa26cef0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350593}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0b12031a-9b3e-5e65-98ec-939654ef6714" :question/math-academy-id "q-71116" :question/problem "Calculate the length of the altitude $ZH$ of the $△\\,WYZ$, if $W(2,3,2)$, $Y(1,2,1)$, $Z(1,-1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the length of the altitude $ZH$ can be related to the area of $△\\,WYZ$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}ZH\\cdot WY\n$$\n\nSo, to find $ZH,$ we first find ${A}_{△}.$ To start, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{WY}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{WZ}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{WY} & =y-w \\\\  & =(i+2j+k)-(2i+3j+2k) \\\\  & =-i-j-k \\\\  & =⟨-1,-1,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{WZ} & =z-w \\\\  & =(i-j+k)-(2i+3j+2k) \\\\  & =-i-4j-k \\\\  & =⟨-1,-4,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{WY}\\times \\overset{\\to }{WZ} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -4 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -4\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-1)\\cdot (-1)-(-4)\\cdot (-1))i-((-1)\\cdot (-1)-(-1)\\cdot (-1))j+((-1)\\cdot (-4)-(-1)\\cdot (-1))k \\\\  & =-3i+3k \\\\  & =⟨-3,0,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{WY}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{WZ}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{WY}\\times \\overset{\\to }{WZ}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{0}^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{18} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,WYZ$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's also compute $WY$ since it appears in the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}WY & =|\\overset{\\to }{WY}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, using the formula ${A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}ZH\\cdot WY,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△} & =\\frac{1}{2}ZH\\cdot WY \\\\ \\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}ZH\\cdot \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 3\\sqrt{2} & =ZH\\cdot \\sqrt{3} \\\\ ZH & =\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ ZH & =\\sqrt{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
